Z||000000||WayneF||10-11-1999||11:15 PM||||I have an 1988 fiero with a 4 cyl and a 1985 chassis with a V6 that I bought for the engine.  Both run great when cold, when operating is reached, the engines run terrible and usually die. I assume they both have the same problem.  Computer reading a bad sensor or what?  The 88 gives a error code of 15 - coolant sensor, The 85 chassis doesn't have the check engine light but I may have to hook one up. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||DJRice||10-12-1999||09:25 AM||||Sounds like they are overheating......  Pull the thermostat and radiator caps off and make sure that the system is full with both of these caps off.  <P>Why does the 85 not have a check engine light?  If you just bought it, then someone pulled the bulb out to hide a problem.....<P>Do a search for Coolant Fill Procedure and see what that turns up, the proper way to fill the cooling system has been discussed many times.||||reg||1
